commit 7afa1dc73a768423ec5d3823e62a58c6d0bd4aeb
Author: Kareem <kareem@wolfssl.com>
Date:   Thu Mar 5 16:34:26 2026 -0700

    Add wolfSSL support to hitch.

    To use it, build wolfSSL with:
    ./autogen.sh
    ./configure --enable-hitch
    make
    sudo make install
    
    Then build hitch with:
    patch -p1 < </path/to/patch/file>
    ./bootstrap --with-wolfssl
    make
    make check-recursive
    
    The bundled tests are adjusted so the suite passes with wolfSSL:
    - test13 connects with TLS 1.2: its cipher list is TLS 1.2-only and
      wolfSSL applies it to TLS 1.3 as well.
    - test15 skips itself when hitch is built without NPN support; wolfSSL
      does not implement NPN (ALPN is covered by test16).
    - test39 accepts the client cert flags wolfSSL reports on a connection
      without a client certificate.  It also requires a wolfSSL where
      PEM_write_bio_X509_AUX() uses the TRUSTED CERTIFICATE PEM armor
      (newer than release 5.9.2); with older wolfSSL its TLV length check
      fails.

    When building from a tree that previously built another hitch version,
    delete any generated src/cfg_lex.c, src/cfg_parser.c and src/cfg_parser.h
    first: the build only regenerates them when missing, and a parser left
    over from another release makes tests 12 and 41 fail on config parse
    errors.

